# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 7 (R3: a dynamic's update event fires at n with the value after n) and ch. 8 (a widget's dynamic parameter is the caller's dynamic): each click writes `$a`, and the widget's `!Updated $c` fires in that tick with the new value.
test a_widget_hears_its_parameter

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="bump")
    1: Ui.Label(text="heard 0, last 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="heard 1, last 1")

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="heard 2, last 2")
